-- title:
--   Principal series map from tame split inertia at q
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a non-zero natural number and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. a normalised eigenform (the $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity on coprime indices and the two recursions at primes away from and dividing $M$) such that no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ carries a normalised eigenform with the same $\ell$-th coefficients for all primes $\ell\nmid M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals, and $\mathcal O'$ a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field in whose maximal ideal $\lambda$ lies, with $\lambda\neq 2$. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathbb Z[T_\ell,U_p]\subseteq\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ (generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_p$ for primes $p\mid M$, $p\notin S$) to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for all such $\ell$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O'$. Let $\rho$ be a $\lambda$-adic Galois representation over $\mathcal O'$: a free $\mathcal O'$-module $V$ of rank two, finite over $\mathcal O'$, with an adically continuous monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O'}(V)$. Assume its residual representation on the residue field is irreducible (every Galois-stable submodule is $\bot$ or $\top$) and odd ($\det$ of every involution other than the identity is $-1$), and that for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$ (acting as $x\mapsto x^\ell$ on the residue field), the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X+\ell$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq\lambda$, $q\equiv-1 \pmod \lambda$ and $\operatorname{ord}_q(M)=2$, let $\Phi$ be a non-zero function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb Q$ which is an adelic lift of $g$ (left invariant under the global points, right invariant under the finite level-one subgroup for the ideal $(M)$, and agreeing with the weight-two slash action of $g$ at $i$ on elements with trivial finite part and positive archimedean determinant). Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit, and assume $\rho(\sigma)=1$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup at $P$ over $\mathbb Q$ that acts trivially on tame quotients, i.e. with $\sigma z\cdot z^{-1}-1$ a non-unit of $P$ for all $z\neq 0$. Finally let $j\colon\mathcal O'\to\mathcal O''$ be an injective ring homomorphism into a domain and $a\colon\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to(\mathcal O'')^\times$ a function such that for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup at $P$ the image under $j$ of the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ equals $(X-a(\sigma))(X-a(\sigma)^{-1})$, such that $a$ is multiplicative on that inertia subgroup, and such that $a(\sigma)^{q-1}=1$ there. Then there exist homomorphisms $\mu_1,\mu_2\colon\mathbb Q_q^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ and a $\mathbb C$-linear map $f$ from the adelic span of $\Phi$ (the span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2$-translates of $\Phi$) to the principal series carrier for $q,\mu_1,\mu_2$ (locally constant functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$ transforming under the Borel subgroup by $\mu_1\otimes\mu_2$ times the half-modulus) such that $f(x\cdot v)=x\cdot f(v)$ for all $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$ and all $v$, and $f\neq 0$.
--
--   This is the local analysis at a prime $q$ with $q^2\,\|\,M$ in the level-lowering step: tame inertia at $q$ acting with split characteristic polynomials of the stated shape forces the local component of the automorphic representation attached to $g$ at $q$ to embed equivariantly into a principal series, rather than being supercuspidal. It is used in the contrapositive form that, when no such non-zero equivariant map to a principal series carrier exists, the inertial labels at $q$ fail the relation $a(\sigma)^{q-1}=1$.
